WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.769
NARRATOR: We are here
to document the lives

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.204
of people living in Alaska.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.272
The harsh reality is the
environment we're up against.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.374
It makes it tough to do our job.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.742
Get out of there!

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.944
NARRATOR: Working on "Life Below
Zero" can be very dangerous.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.078
Gun's here.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:12.879
Camera's here.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:13.747
Never know what to expect.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:14.547
ALASKAN 1: Hey, hey!

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.615
You [bleep] that.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.716
NARRATOR: It's
going to be tough,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.718
but we're going to get the shot.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:21.221
Every scenario, we've
got to prepare for this.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.422
ALASKAN 2: But
we're still smiling.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.590
We're having fun.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.226
Still making "Life Below Zero."

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.327
Yes.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.128
Bring it on.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.063
[theme music]

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.746
TERRY PRATT: Well,
we're back at Andy's.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.416
Now we got to get
the necessities

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.017
for us, which is some heat.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:54.287
We're expecting temperatures
anywhere from minus 20, 30.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.890
When it gets this cold, you
burn a lot of wood to stay warm.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.762
BRET BOHN: We're going
to drop this tree

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.831
right down there is the
plan, in between these two

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.132
big spruces here.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.734
TERRY PRATT: You don't want
to just cut down any tree.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.569
You need to find a good
dead tree, that standing

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:14.874
dead tree which is nice dry wood
which will burn like a monster.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.776
[chain saw revving]

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.616
[bleep] This is not good.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.818
TERRY PRATT: What are you doing?

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.053
It's kind of leaning
towards that crotch there.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.087
TERRY PRATT: Oh, [bleep].

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.222
Oh, it's going to
have enough weight.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.090
It's going to punch
right through it, bro.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.126
I'm going to try to cut
it over here and leave all

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.394
the wood over here
and try to put it

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:35.528
right where I want it, though.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.329
TERRY PRATT: All right.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:39.899
[chain saw revving]

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:40.700
There it is.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.634
Yeah, buddy.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.006
Timber.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.508
Well, I got it on that side.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.844
Yeah, you did.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.911
Boom.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.279
Took it down.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.215
And that literally,
that one tree

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.685
is going to keep us going
for probably nearly a week.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.719
It depends how cold it gets.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.961
TERRY PRATT: So Bret just
felled quite a big tree.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.163
He's bucking it up now until
like eight foot lengths.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.265
I'm going to pull
the snowmobile around

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.900
and just start loading it up.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.202
And we hope to get
it 3, 4 feet high.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.506
Before we can get comfy
and start our filming here,

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.709
we need to be able to have
enough heat to maintain us

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.711
for a couple of days, at least,
before we have to stop again

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.712
and replenish our supplies.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.818
I think Andy's going
to be impressed.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:32.619
That's all I have to say.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:43.696
As you can see, one tree
really does the job, huh, Bret?

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.231
We aren't even done
with that tree, right?

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.399
Another load like
this, probably.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.333
No, we do.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.301
We have another
load [inaudible]..

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.875
It was hard work,
knee deep in the snow,

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.944
and hefting these
logs on your shoulders

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.112
and moving them around.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:00.446
At least we can
start up a roaring

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.414
fire right when we get back.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.052
It's cold.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.186
It's unpredictable.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.454
And we don't know what
we're going to get here.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.323
This is the challenge
of working in the Arctic.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.864
SIMEON HOUTMAN: We are
currently in [inaudible]..

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:23.136
We're out filming Sue as she
takes her generator to Chevak.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.238
This is the crew one that
we're filming in right now.

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.674
But we've literally
got three miles in

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.108
and we've just got it stuck.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.444
So it's going to
be a long journey.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.746
But first things first.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.649
We're going to need to help
get this thing unstuck.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.017
It's cold out.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:38.785
Warm up, boys.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:45.291
As you can see, we
are pretty much stuck.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.660
We have come out
with two tuckers.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.529
This is the river right here.

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.631
And we just sunk into
some serious overflow.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:52.865
So Sue's the one
who is going to have

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.335
to try and get us out
right now because obviously

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.104
we ain't going nowhere.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.305
That's pretty deep.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.640
Actually, not entirely
sure whether it

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:01.708
was going to get out at all.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.048
The wind's picking up.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.317
It's about minus 15 right now.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:14.120
They need to get it out of here
before it freezes in there.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:18.091
Otherwise, it ain't
moving at all.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.460
There's a big rush
against time right now.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.962
So they're going to try and
dig out all the excess snow

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.297
and going to get
it out there quick.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.164
See all this overflow?

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.532
If it freezes, it ain't moving.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:32.105
[dramatic music]

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.611
Wahoo!

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:39.979
We got it out.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.114
Freaking awesome.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.715
Look at that hole it made.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.817
That's a sinkhole right there.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.252
ROB POLLARD: So
just a few minutes

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.388
ago, this was fully submerged.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:53.226
So it got a bunch of snow
piled up inside this track.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:57.764
You got to free this up so
that this thing could move

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.200
and the track could do its job.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:04.070
All that snow is off this track.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:08.841
They'll have roughly 70
miles to go in this journey.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:13.246
So hopefully, we'll just be
able to carry on to Chevak, pray

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:15.515
that we don't run
into any more overflow

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:18.251
or any other obstacles.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:21.754
Last thing you want is to be
stuck in the middle of nowhere.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.356
Hopefully, we can just
keep chugging along

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:26.659
and get to Chevak and
finish out our story.

